    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>An inland Javanese sultanate founded by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/panembahan-senapati">Panembahan Senapati</a> around 1587, built on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rice">rice</a> lands of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/central-java">Central Java</a>.</li><li><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sultan-agung">Sultan Agung</a> conquered the coastal states, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/madura">Madura</a> and Surabaya, but twice failed to take <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch">Dutch</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/batavia">Batavia</a>, in 1628 and 1629.</li><li>Rebellion and succession wars made it dependent on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch">Dutch</a>, and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-giyanti">Treaty of Giyanti</a> split it in two in 1755.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sultan-agung">Sultan Agung</a>’s <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/javanese-calendar">Javanese calendar</a> of 1633 kept the old Saka year count but switched to Islamic lunar months; it is still used for court ceremonies in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/java">Java</a>.</p></aside>
    </section>

